<!--
  The API's reader: the account every API screen reads ClickHouse with (F20, NFR14,
  ADR-045). The scheduler keeps `nexovue_reader` (reader.xml), so its alert and
  detection reads sit outside this account's bounds.

  Why a second reader. The API's own caps (dashboard scans per process, the batch's
  permits) protect its connections, and nothing else: at two API processes, dashboards
  and every other screen together could hold several 1 GiB reads at once, and the
  server's cap (config.d/memory.xml) fails every query when it is reached, the
  workers' inserts and the alert sweeps included. These two bounds are the server's,
  so they hold across processes and whatever the code sends:

  - max_memory_usage_for_user: what all of this account's running reads may hold
    together. 2.4 GiB, a guess (design, *Performance and scale*), below the server's
    cap so the scheduler and the inserts keep room. Over it, a read fails with
    MEMORY_LIMIT_EXCEEDED (241), which a dashboard panel reads as `failed`.
  - max_concurrent_queries_for_user: how many of its reads run at once. 12, a guess,
    below the 16 connections two API processes hold. Over it, a read is refused with
    TOO_MANY_SIMULTANEOUS_QUERIES (202), which a dashboard panel reads as `refused`.

  Both names were read on the pinned 26.3 image (system.settings) before use. Both
  values are guesses until the feature's measurement (plan T5.7) sets them.

  Otherwise exactly the reader's profile: readonly = 2, because every read sends its
  bounds as query settings, and constraints, because readonly = 2 would let a query
  raise them. The two per-user bounds are const, so no query can lift them.
-->
<clickhouse>
  <profiles>
    <api_reader>
      <readonly>2</readonly>
      <max_memory_usage>1073741824</max_memory_usage>
      <max_bytes_before_external_group_by>536870912</max_bytes_before_external_group_by>
      <max_execution_time>30</max_execution_time>
      <max_memory_usage_for_user>2576980378</max_memory_usage_for_user>
      <max_concurrent_queries_for_user>12</max_concurrent_queries_for_user>
      <constraints>
        <max_memory_usage>
          <min>1</min>
          <max>1073741824</max>
        </max_memory_usage>
        <max_execution_time>
          <min>1</min>
          <max>30</max>
        </max_execution_time>
        <max_memory_usage_for_user>
          <const/>
        </max_memory_usage_for_user>
        <max_concurrent_queries_for_user>
          <const/>
        </max_concurrent_queries_for_user>
      </constraints>
    </api_reader>
  </profiles>

  <users>
    <nexovue_api_reader>
      <password from_env="CLICKHOUSE_API_READER_PASSWORD"/>
      <profile>api_reader</profile>
      <quota>default</quota>
      <networks>
        <ip>::/0</ip>
      </networks>
      <grants>
        <query>GRANT SELECT ON nexovue.*</query>
      </grants>
    </nexovue_api_reader>
  </users>
</clickhouse>
